      "message": "Great !\nMeanwhile we are finally able to load the *.wasm* module with some minor changes in the generated JS. Updated the artifacts here, https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1OZpr6JDtLOz4jKqUXsdEe8t9rtzkJce3\n\nNow, the critical part would be how to initialize the HelloWorld object and invoke the functions from JS/HTML ?\nThe native Application::Create/HelloWorld Ctor needs the *platformData*, I wonder how should we provide it from JS/HTML. Should we change the C++ interfaces, to accept something like a *canvas* (but again, they should be consistent across all sk_app backends)?\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/example/HelloWorld.cpp;l\u003d29\nWe would need your inputs, to do something like https://github.com/google/skia/blob/main/demos.skia.org/demos/hello_world/index.html or how Box2D/Bullet(ammo.js) does.\nLooking forward, Thanks.",
